# 164.7-03 — NEUTER EVIDENCE

Phase 164.7 / plan 03. Nine assertions, each NEUTERED and observed RED before
being committed, each restored and verified.

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Every gate in this plan is either an absence assertion or
an equality against extracted text, and both are green over an empty derivation.
An assertion nobody has watched FAIL is indistinguishable from one that cannot.

WHAT IS PROVEN, and by which oracle:

| # | neuter | oracle |
|---|--------|--------|
| N1 | the NULL-safe comparison broken, two ways | lane tracer (T-a) + the migration's own verify |
| N2 | the read handler assigns TRUE, not NULL | lane tracer (T-c) |
| N3 | the guard moved below the advisory lock | pytest gate 4 (the migration's verify is BLIND, by design) |
| N4 | the seed set TRUE / check (7) deleted | lane tracer (T-b) + the migration's own verify |
| N-P1 | `IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE` -> `<> TRUE` | pytest gate 4 |
| N-P2 | handler assigns TRUE instead of NULL | pytest gate 4 |
| N-P3 | a statement inserted before the guard | pytest gate 4 |
| N-P4 | the read deleted (0 reads) | pytest gate 4 |
| N-P5 | `IF NOT v_enabled THEN` | pytest gate 4 |
| N-P6 | a NULL-unsafe spelling ADDED beside a correct guard | pytest gate 4 |

⭐ N1 and N3 are the two that say something the plan did not already assume:

  * N1(a) shows the migration's OWN verify block catches the crude swap before
    the tracer ever runs — two defences, and the outer one fires first. N1(b)
    then defeats that text check with an edit that KEEPS the token and is still
    NULL-unsafe (`IS NOT NULL AND …`), and only the behavioural arm sees it.
    That pair is the argument for having both layers, measured rather than
    asserted.
  * N3 is the mirror: a guard in the WRONG PLACE satisfies every text check the
    migration makes about itself, and only the pytest position assertion sees
    it. Each layer catches what the other cannot.

  * N-P6 exists for the same reason at the assertion level: N-P5 reddens on the
    POSITIVE comparison assertion, so on its own it would leave the
    must-not-appear list unproven. N-P6 keeps a correct guard and adds a
    NULL-unsafe spelling beside it, which only that list can catch.

